--TEST--
An `@param` that names no parameter of its function is `E0335`, and the fix renames it when exactly one parameter is undocumented — `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-closed-and-checked`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `@param` names a parameter of the function it documents.
final class Ledger {
    /// Adds one entry.
    ///
    /// @param $amount the amount to add
    /// @param $note a note nothing declares
    public static function add(int $amount): int {
        return $amount;
    }

    /// Takes one entry away.
    ///
    /// @param $amount the amount to take away
    /// @param $why the reason it is taken away
    public static function remove(int $amount, string $reason): int {
        return -$amount;
    }
}
echo Ledger::add(3), "\n";
echo Ledger::remove(2, "refund"), "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0335]: `@param` names `$note`, which is not a parameter here
  --> %s:7:16
  |
7 |     /// @param $note a note nothing declares
  |                ^^^^^ no such parameter
  = suggestion: delete the `@param` line (delete)

error[E0335]: `@param` names `$why`, which is not a parameter here
   --> %s:15:16
   |
15 |     /// @param $why the reason it is taken away
   |                ^^^^ no such parameter
   = suggestion: rename the tag to the undocumented parameter: `$reason`

error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
